packetdrill is a scriptable network stack testing tool.  It can test
TCP, UDP, UDPLite, SCTP, IPv4 and IPv6 behavior from the system call
layer down to the wire.  This package is based on the nplab fork, which
adds SCTP/UDPLite support and improved BSD support.

packetdrill needs root privileges and a tun(4) device to run tests.
